<p>
    I got a Trinitron KV-36XBR200 a month or so back. Thing's an absolute unit. The chrominance on composite/S-Video
    inputs doesn't seem to quite work on the main output (works fine in picture-in-picture/picture-and-picture) so I
    decided to do an RGB mod to work around that issue in the meantime.
</p>
<p>
    I got a mod kit from <a href="https://sunthar.com/crts/sony/sony-kv-36xbr200" target="_blank">Sunthar</a> for the
    similar KV-27V20 and a copy of <a href="https://archive.org/details/manual_KV36XBR200_SM_SONY" target="_blank">the
        service manual from archive.org</a>. I would have zero clue how to do any of this otherwise.
</p>

<h2 linkable>Assembling the Board</h2>
<p>
    Populating the mod board itself was easy because everything was through-hole and all of the resistors, diodes, and
    transistors needed were known and documented on Sunthar's site. I went back and added a bit more solder to the parts
    here that were a bit low before installing the board - my eyes are definitely starting to have a harder time
    catching this stuff.
</p>
